details:
(a) whether Wage Agreement for BSNL Non-Executives, signed on 08.10.2025 after negotiations with recognised unions and approved by BSNL Board, remains pending for implementation;
(b) whether the Affordability Clause impedes implementation of 3rd PRC despite three Revival Packages and BSNL’s improved financial performance;
(c) whether a special exemption of Affordability Clause would be granted considering BSNL's strategic importance;
(d) whether consultations were held with DPE, DoT and BSNL during the last two years regarding 3rd PRC and if so, the outcomes thereof; and
(e) the timeline and any special dispensation proposed to implement wage revision with effect from 01.01.2017, considering BSNL's strategic national role?

(a) current status of construction of Thiruvananthapuram Outer Ring Road;
(b) what was the original timeframe for the completion of the project;
(c) what is the current bottleneck in this project;
(d) whether it is a fact that thousands of landowners affected by the Vizhinjam–Navaikulam Outer Ring Road project have been complaining prolonged delays in compensation despite surrendering their land;
(e) if so, reasons therefor; and
(f) new timelines within which the project will be completed?

(a) whether Thiruvananthapuram-Angamaly Greenfield highway project has been cancelled;
(b) if so, whether Government will revive it with alignment changes to exclude commercial and residential areas;
(c) the current status of upgradation of roads between Kannur and Mysore as National Highways;
(d) whether Kerala sought exemption from sharing 25 percent land acquisition cost for Chovva-Mattannur-Virajapetta-Madikkeri-Mysore road works, Ernakulam Bypass and Kollam-Shenkoattai roads; 
(e) whether NHAI will take actions to secure alignment approval for the portion of Mysore-Malappuram Greenfield Corridor falling in Karnataka and to reinclude the project under any suitable schemes; and
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) total amount lying in inoperative and unclaimed bank accounts as on 30 June 2026, bank-wise;
(b) total amount transferred to the Depositor Education and Awareness Fund till date, bank-wise;
(c) the amount refunded to rightful claimants till date; and
(d) the measures taken to facilitate speedy settlement of claims?
vg

(a) whether Government is considering any amendment or relaxation of the existing policy restricting operators of major airports from holding substantial equity in or operating, scheduled airlines;
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government received any representation from airport operators or other stakeholders seeking such relaxation;
(d) whether Government has assessed the impact of such cross-ownership on competition, conflict of interest, slot allocation, airport charges, ground handling and fair access to airport infrastructure for competing airlines;
(e) whether the views of the Competition Commission of India, DGCA and Airports Authority of India have been obtained thereon; and
(f) if so, the details thereof?
vg

(a) whether Government has finalised the allocation of Vande Bharat sleeper train services;
(b) the criteria adopted for selection of routes and allocation of train sets;
(c) whether Kerala has been identified for any such service;
(d) if so, the details thereof, including the proposed routes, frequency and expected date of commencement;
(e) whether Government has received requests for introducing Vande Bharat sleeper services on the Thiruvananthapuram–Bengaluru, Thiruvananthapuram–Chennai, Thiruvananthapuram–Mangaluru, Kozhikode–Chennai and other long-distance overnight routes; and
(f) if so, the details thereof and the action taken thereon?

(a) whether Government has decided to directly allocate spectrum for satellite-based internet broadband services;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government intends to provide subsidy for satellite based broadband services from Digital Bharat Nidhi; and
(d) whether similar spectrum-access terms and subsidy mechanisms would be uniformly extended to all conventional communication operators including BSNL?

(a) total number of children reported missing, traced and recovered during each of the last five years, State-wise and UT-wise;
(b) total number of missing children who remain untraced during each of the last five years, State-wise and UT-wise;
(c) whether Government has observed any increase in the incidents of missing children in recent years;
(d) if so, the details thereof along with the reasons identified; and
(e) details of the agencies, institutional mechanisms and initiatives in place for tracing and recovering missing children, including the coordination framework among the police, child protection authorities and other concerned agencies?

(a) the number of ration cards deleted, suspended or restored during the last five years, State-wise;
(b) whether any independent audit has been conducted regarding exclusion of beneficiaries owing to Aadhaar authentication or technological failures;
(c) the number of grievances received on this account; and
(d) the corrective measures taken to ensure that no eligible beneficiary is denied foodgrains under the National Food Security Act?

(a) number of posts filled under General-PwD category in faculty recruitment at the Indian Statistical Institute (ISI), from the level of Assistant Professor onwards, during 2020–2025;
(b) number of appointments made pursuant to directions of the Commissioner for Persons with Disabilities under General-PwD categories during 2020-2025;
(c) details thereof;
(d) number of General-PwD candidates provided equal opportunity in faculty recruitment during 2020–2025;
(e) steps taken to ensure recruitment of PwD candidates based on seniority, experience and equal opportunity across all ISI units; and
(f) number of recruitment advertisements during the period in which PwD candidates were not called for interview?

(a) number and details of safety violations and technical defects identified in domestic and international flight operations during the last three years;
(b) whether Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) has detected multiple violations related to airlines, airports, aircraft maintenance works, etc., during its surveillance at major airports post Ahmedabad aircraft crash;
(c) if so, number of such violations detected and the details thereof;
(d) the number of show cause notices that were issued with respect to safety violations during the last three years;
(e) responses received from flight carriers and the actions taken so far; and
(f) number and details of the completed disciplinary or enforcement actions taken in this regard?

(a) whether the Rail Coach Factory at Kanjikode, sanctioned in Budget 2008-09 and for which foundation stone was laid in 2012, remains unimplemented despite acquisition of land by Government of Kerala;
(b) if so, the reasons therefor, including whether the subsequent PPP model and review of coach manufacturing capacity led to its deferment;
(c) whether Government proposes to revive the project or establish any alternative railway manufacturing facility at the site; and
(d) the present status of the project, land acquired, expenditure incurred and the timeline for a final decision?

(a) whether sanction of Detailed Project Report (DPR) surveys for normal rail corridors signifies a shift from a dedicated semi high-speed corridor to incremental speed enhancement of existing railway network in Kerala;
(b) whether the Railway Minister has recently stated that the proposed additional lines from Mangaluru to Shoranur and Shoranur to Kanyakumari could reduce Thiruvananthapuram–Kasaragod travel time by four hours;
(c) the status, cost, land requirement and implementation timeline thereof;
(d) the status of currently pending high speed/ semi high speed rail projects including the project proposed by Dr. E. Sreedharan; and 
(e) the steps taken to provide Kerala time-bound integrated high-speed rail connectivity?

(a) the number of permanent and contract/temporary workers employed in factories and other establishments, as per EPFO, ESIC and other available data, State-wise and year-wise for the last five years;
(b) the number of establishments that reported retrenchment, lay-offs, closures or lock-outs during the last three years, State-wise, with the number of workers affected; 
(c) the sector-wise details of major retrenchments reported during the period and the reasons therefor; and
(d) the statutory and administrative mechanisms to safeguard the wages, social security, continuity of employment and service conditions of employees including contract and temporary workers?

(a) the number of Indian seafarers and other Indian nationals killed, injured, stranded or evacuated due to the ongoing conflict in the Middle East since January, 2026, country-wise;
(b) the details of compensation and assistance provided to them or their families;
(c) the diplomatic actions taken pursuant to such incidents; and
(d) whether the Ministry proposes a dedicated crisis protection and insurance mechanism for Indians working in conflict-prone regions?
vg

(a) total quantum of net Foreign Direct Investment inflows received by India during the FYs 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 and 2025-26, year wise, State-wise and category-wise;
(b) the quantum of FDI outflows, including repatriation, disinvestment and other outward remittances by foreign investors, during the said period, year wise; 
(c) whether Government has examined the reasons for the increase in FDI outflows and the consequent impact on net FDI inflows; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of States which requested Union Government to increase tide-over allocation of foodgrains;
(b) the details thereof and response thereto;
(c) whether the continued use of 2011 Census data for NFSA coverage has affected State-wise foodgrain allocations;
(d) the details thereof and response thereto;
(e) whether Government proposes to enhance the priority household coverage in Kerala based on Aadhaar-seeded beneficiaries; and
(f) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the National Dam Safety Authority has removed Kerala's representative from the Independent Expert Committee constituted for the Comprehensive Dam Safety Evaluation of the Mullaperiyar Dam;
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government of Kerala was consulted prior to such removal;
(d) the present composition of the Committee, indicating the State-wise representation of its members; and
(e) measures taken to ensure adequate representation of Kerala in bodies entrusted with evaluating the safety of the Mullaperiyar Dam?

(a) whether States including Kerala are repeatedly objecting the mandatory PMAY-Urban logo display on beneficiary houses citing dignity, privacy, self-respect of economically weaker beneficiaries and federal concerns; 
(b) if so, whether Government will review its insistence on permanent branding on homes under PMAY-U 2.0;
(c) the total amount allocated and outstanding to Kerala under PMAY-U during the last five years; and
(d) the details thereof and reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has directed Broadcast Audience Research Council (BARC) to suspend publication of television audience ratings across all genres pending registration under the Television Ratings Policy, 2026; 
(b) if so, the reasons therefor and the likely timeline for resumption of ratings; 
(c) whether Government proposes to permit multiple television rating agencies under the new policy;
(d) whether Government will have any role in the selection, registration, recognition, regulation or removal of such agencies;
(e) safeguards to ensure the agencies functional and operational independence; and
(f) major changes introduced under the Television Ratings Policy, 2026 to improve transparency, competition, sample coverage and the credibility of television audience measurement?

(a) whether Government took a final decision on implementation of the recommendations of Kasturirangan Committee relating to declaration of Ecologically Sensitive Areas (ESA)) in Western Ghats;
(b) the present status of proposal relating to Kerala, including the extent of area and number of villages proposed to be notified as ESA;
(c) whether Kerala sought modification of the proposed ESA boundaries in view of the large population residing in the affected areas and mapping discrepancies;
(d) if so, the response of Government thereto; and
(e) whether Government proposes to issue the final notification only after resolving the concerns raised by the State Governments and local communities?

(a) whether earlier Indian passports expressly carried the endorsement "Citizen of India", thereby recording the holder's citizenship;
(b) if so, when and why was such endorsement discontinued from Indian passports; 
(c) whether the Ministry will clarify that deletion from electoral roll or similar administrative action under any other statute shall not, by itself, constitute a ground to question the citizenship of an existing passport holder or refuse renewal of passport;
(d) whether the Ministry or any agency under its administrative control has sought, received or used data generated during the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) for processing passport applications or renewals; and 
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) total annual allocation of foodgrains under various categories to each State during the last three years, State-wise, year-wise and category-wise;
(b) whether Government proposed any amendment to the National Food Security Act or the Antyodaya Anna Yojana affecting existing entitlement of foodgrains to beneficiary households and consequential allocation to States;
(c) whether the proposed reduction in free foodgrain entitlement for households with fewer than five members would disproportionately affect States like Kerala, where small nuclear families predominate; and
(d) whether Kerala Government submitted any formal representation regarding the proposed changes in allocation, details thereof and response thereto?

(a) the quantum and details of debt of the Union Government as on date;
(b) the details of debt during the last five years, year-wise and category-wise;
(c) the debt to GDP ratio during the last five years;
(d) the ratio of debt service to fresh debt receipts during that period;
(e) the Current Account Deficit of the Country during last five financial years, year-wise;
(f) the Fiscal Deficit of the Union Government during last five years; and
(g) the ratio of Fiscal Deficit to the GDP during that period?

(a) the number of companies against which action has been initiated during the last five years for non-disclosure of Significant Beneficial Ownership (SBO), State-wise;
(b) the number of companies struck off during the said period;
(c) whether the Ministry will take steps to make suitable amendments in the Acts administered by the Ministry so as to define what an offshore shell company is;
(d) whether any actions have been taken by the Ministry to collect the details of offshore shell companies whose Ultimate Beneficial Ownership (UBO) are held by Indian citizens; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government received complaints from vehicle manufacturers, automobile associations, consumer organisations, etc., regarding engine failure, fuel pump issues, reduced fuel efficiency, corrosion, water contamination or other performance issues allegedly associated with E20 ethanol-blended petrol;
(b) number of such complaints received during the last three years, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) whether Oil Companies have issued advisories cautioning motorists regarding water contamination in ethanol-blended petrol and its possible effects on vehicles; and
(d) the basis and criteria on which Government concluded, in its PIB release dated 23rd June 2026, that 'no widespread issues’ of engine failure or vehicle breakdown attributable to ethanol blending have been reported?

(a) present status of the investigation into the Ahmedabad airplane crash;
(b) whether final investigation report has been delayed beyond the indicative timeline of one year under ICAO norms;
(c) whether Government received any representations alleging that selective disclosure of cockpit voice recorder extracts in the preliminary report led to speculation regarding the cause of the accident or the conduct of the flight crew;
(d) reasons therefor and response thereto;
(e) whether Government has received any representations or complaints from victims' families, pilot associations or other stakeholders regarding the conduct, transparency or methodology of the investigation; and
(f) details thereof and action taken thereon?

(a) whether employees and pensioners of the Employees’ Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO) come under the ambit of the Employees' Pension Scheme (EPS);
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether EPFO employees had earlier been covered under EPS and were subsequently shifted to Government pension scheme and if so, the details thereof;
(e) the average monthly pension received by retired EPFO employees during the last one year;
(f) the average annual pension paid to EPFO pensioners during that period; and
(g) the quantum of pension and other retirement benefits disbursed to EPFO employees during that period?

(a) the details and quantum of unclaimed amount available with the Department of Posts under various savings/ deposits schemes;
(b) the quantum and details of amounts so far transferred by the Department to the Senior Citizen Welfare Fund (SCWF);
(c) the quantum and details of unclaimed amount available with the Department as on date and not transferred to SCWF, which remains unclaimed for a period not exceeding ten years from the due date; and
(d) the quantum and year-wise details of unclaimed amounts repaid to the deposit holders/ legal heirs after its transfer to SCWF?

(a) total number of students who committed suicide in higher educational institutions and tuition centres during last three years;
(b) year-wise, State-wise, and category-wise (male and female, Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes, Other Backward Classes, and General Category) details thereof; and
(c) reasons identified for these suicides, details thereof?

(a) actual expenditure by Union Government on education during the last five years as percentage of GDP;
(b) year-wise and State-wise details thereof;
(c) actual expenditure by State Governments on education during the last five years as percentage of GSDP;
(d) year-wise and State-wise details thereof;
(e) year-wise growth rate in Union Budget allocations for Education during the last five years, and the extent to which such growth, in real terms, has kept pace with inflation; and
(f) year-wise details thereof?

(a) total number of LPG connections that have been provided under the Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana (PMUY) since its inception;
(b) the details thereof, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) State-wise average annual consumption of LPG cylinders by PMUY beneficiaries and the corresponding average annual consumption by non-PMUY domestic consumers;
(d) the details and quantum of Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) subsidy disbursed to domestic LPG consumers during the last five years; and
(e) the details thereof, State-wise and year-wise?
bpn

(a) the details of the scholarship schemes currently available for the minority students at all stages of education;
(b) the number of beneficiaries, State-wise;
(c) the total scholarship amount earmarked and total amount disbursed per annum for minority students during the last five years, State-wise;
(d) the names and details of scholarship schemes discontinued or merged during the last five years;
(e) the amount allocated to the Ministry in Budgets, its RE allocation and Actuals during the said period;
(f) the amounts actually spent by Government during the last five years; and
(g) the details thereof, year-wise and State-wise?

(a) the year-wise details, in absolute monetary terms (in ?), of the total revenue earned by the Railways during the last five years up to 31.12.2025, on account of Flexi Fare, Tatkal charges, Premium Tatkal charges and cancellation charges on tickets;
(b) the total revenue collected, in rupee terms, under each of the above categories during the said period; and
(c) year-wise and category-wise details thereof?

(a) details and objectives of subsidies under Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme;
(b) whether objectives such as employment generation, net domestic value addition, export obligations, etc., are prescribed for PLI subsidies;
(c) total PLI allocation and amount expended so far by Government with sector-wise break up;
(d) employment generation realised, sector-wise;
(e) details of beneficiaries under the scheme;
(f) selection criteria of beneficiaries when multiple firms applied in a particular field of manufacturing; and
(g) State wise details of foreign companies which migrated to India by availing/anticipating to avail benefits under PLI Scheme?

(a) current share of the Central Government in the monthly honorarium of mid-day meal workers and helpers in schools under PM POSHAN;
(b) current actual contribution of State Governments in the monthly honorarium being paid to mid-day meal workers and helpers in schools under PM POSHAN;
(c) State-wise and category-wise details thereof;
(d) whether Union Government will take steps to increase its contribution in the honorarium of mid-day meal workers and helpers in schools, considering that several States, including Kerala, have already enhanced their share of the contribution on multiple occasions; and
(e) if not, reasons therefor and details thereof?

(a) the number of cases involving loan accounts of ?50 crore and above resolved under the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code during the last three years till 31.12.2025 and the total amount of haircuts taken by banks in such cases, year-wise;
(b) whether banks have also resorted to the practice of "greening the debt" by sanctioning fresh loans to service existing stressed loans of ?50 crore and above during the same period;
(c) if so, the number of such cases and the total amount involved, year-wise; and
(d) the steps taken by Government and regulators to curb such practices?
J

(a) the number and details of hospitals de-empanelled and penalised under the Ayushman Bharat - PMJAY scheme during the last five years, details thereof, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the main grounds for such de-empanelment, including fraud, overbilling and procedural violations;
(c) the total amount involved therein;
(d) the total amount recovered in such cases till date;
(e) the penalties imposed and recovered in such cases till date; and
(f) the measures taken to strengthen monitoring, prevent misuse of public funds and ensure uninterrupted access to quality healthcare for beneficiaries?
bpn

(a) whether Government proposes to introduce appropriate regulatory measures, including the imposition of fare caps on Middle East routes, to curb seasonal profiteering and prevent predatory pricing or oligopolistic practices by airlines, on the lines of the action taken in imposing immediate caps on domestic airfares following the IndiGo operational disruption;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) total number and details of Free Trade Agreements (FTAs) that India has signed in the last five years;
(b) the details of the agreements which were already in force;
(c) annual trade surplus or trade deficit between India and its FTA partners during last five years;
(d) year-wise and FTA-wise details thereof;
(e) details of trade agreements currently under negotiation, including their present status; and
(f) whether any existing agreements have been identified for review, if so, the reasons and the proposed process of review?

(a) quantum and details of the meat export from India during the last five years, the details thereof, State-wise and category-wise;
(b) quantity of beef, buffalo and other categories of meat exported from India during the last five years, the details thereof, year-wise, State-wise and category-wise; and
(c) details of revenue earned from meat export during the last five years, the details thereof, year-wise, State-wise and category-wise?

(a) the present status of India’s commitments and operations at Chabahar port amid regional conflicts and evolving United States sanctions;
(b) whether US sanctions or conditional waivers have altered India’s funding, equipment transfers or operational decisions relating to Chabahar Port;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether the Central Government has abandoned or paused the project;
(e) if so, the details thereof; and
(f) if not, the details of steps being taken to safeguard India’s strategic and commercial interests at Chabahar Port?
v

(a) the number of Indian nationals presently residing in West Asian countries, including Israel, Iran, Iraq and the Gulf region;
(b) ????whether any Indian nationals have been affected, stranded or displaced due to prevailing security situation, in view of the ongoing hostilities involving Israel, the United States and Iran;
(c) ????the advisories and contingency measures, including evacuation plans, activated by Government; and
????(d) the steps taken to ensure the safety and protection of Indian citizens in the region?

(a) total number of persons died or sustained injuries while cleaning sewers, manholes, septic tanks and other drainage systems across the country during last five years, year-wise and State-wise details thereof;
(b) number of such persons belonging to Scheduled Castes and Other Backward Classes, the details thereof;
(c) number of cases in which compensation was paid to the victims or their families and the amount paid, State-wise details thereof; and
(d) steps taken to ensure provision and mandatory use of safety equipments, mechanisation of cleaning operations and accountability of agencies engaging such workers?

(a) whether IBPS still insists candidates to ensure that they maintain a healthy credit history at the time of joining the participating banks and the minimum credit score will be as per the policy of participating banks;
(b) the number of candidates selected through IBPS whose appointments were cancelled or offers withdrawn for CIBIL/credit-history reasons during the last three years bank-wise; and
(c) whether Government take steps to ensure that educational/medical loans and bona fide indebtedness of poor and middle-class applicants are not treated as disqualifying factors for public sector bank employment?

(a) the quantity of rice and broken rice allocated or sold by the Food Corporation of India (FCI) in open market as well as for ethanol production for biofuel during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the average annual price per kilogram for such sales to States, open market and for ethanol production, category-wise;
(c) the total revenue generated from these sales during last five years, category-wise; and
(d) the details of States that have requested permission to utilise surplus/unutilised portion of allocated rice or to increase the tide over allocation of foodgrains during the last five years?

(a) whether it is a fact that ‘Metroman’ has submitted a new proposal to Government for a high-speed railway corridor connecting Kannur and Thiruvananthapuram;
(b) if so, the details of the proposal, including the proposed alignment, estimated cost, funding pattern and projected timeline;
(c) whether Government has examined the said proposal; and
(d) if so, the stand of Government towards the proposal?

(a) whether there were any changes in the earlier Detailed Project Report (DPR) submitted to Railway Board for sanction on 02.11.2021 vis-à-vis the final DPR submitted by Southern Railway in 2022-23 and sanctioned in April 2023, for new coaching terminal in Nemom;
(b) whether the initial DPR proposed five pit lines and ten stabling lines, whereas the approved DPR provides only two pit lines and three stabling lines;
(c) if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) details of the works dropped or scaled-down in the approved final DPR vis-à-vis the earlier DPR submitted to Railway Board for sanction on 02.11.2021?

(a) whether Government recently advised States including Kerala to review and discontinue bonus over and above Minimum Support Price (MSP) for paddy and wheat;
(b) if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether any assessment has been made of the impact of discontinuation of incentives on farmers, especially when prevailing MSP rates are often inadequate to meet rising input costs, inflation and cost of living;
(d) the remedial measures proposed to protect paddy and wheat farmers’ incomes; and
(e) whether Government is considering demands of States like Kerala for a State-specific MSP framework and to revise the MSP for paddy to ? 40 per kilogram?

(a) the sanctioned strength and vacancies of judges in High Courts and Supreme Court, as on date;
(b) the number of proposals currently pending with Supreme Court collegium or Government;
(c) the vacancies of judges in High Courts which are yet to be recommended by High Court collegiums to Government;
(d) the number of women judges and judges hailing from SC, ST and OBC communities in Supreme Court and High Courts, as on date, State-wise and category-wise; and
(e) the details of current representation of SC, ST and OBCs in the non-judicial staff of Supreme Court and High Courts, as on date, category-wise?

(a) the sanctioned strength and the number of vacancies in the Indian Foreign Service (IFS), as on date;
(b) the number and representation of Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes and Other Backward Classes in the Service, category-wise, as on date; and
(c) the details of officers appointed to the Service during the last five years, year-wise and category-wise (General, SC, ST, OBC and EWS)?

(a) names and details of scholarship schemes currently administered by Ministry for students from Scheduled Castes and other backward communities at all stages of education;
(b) number of beneficiaries, State-wise details thereof;
(c) total scholarship amount proposed and total amount disbursed annually in last five years, State-wise;
(d) names and details of scholarship schemes discontinued or merged during last five years;
(e) amount allocated to Ministry in budgets, its Revised Estimate (RE) allocation and actual expenditure during last five years; and
(f) amount allocated for scholarship schemes, it’s Revised Estimate allocation and amounts actually spent by Ministry during last five years, year-wise details thereof?

(a) total number of permanent regular employees currently working in National Testing Agency(NTA), category-wise details thereof;
(b) total number of contractual, outsourced and temporary personnel engaged by NTA, category-wise details thereof;
(c) total number and details of public examinations being conducted by NTA;
(d) whether Government has assessed the adequacy of NTA’s human resources in light of repeated concerns regarding delays, paper leaks and examination security;
(e) whether Government concur with the adverse observations in the recent report of the Parliamentary Standing Committee on EWCY&S on the NTA; and
(f) steps taken to strengthen in-house capacity, transparency and accountability of the NTA?
bpn

(a) the gross tax and non-tax revenue of the Union Government from 2021 till date, year-wise;
(b) the net divisible pool vertically devolved to States from 2021 till date, year-wise; 
(c) the Cess and Surcharges excluding GST Compensation Cess and cost of collection of taxes collected from 2021 till date, year-wise;
(d) the quantum and percentage-wise share of Cesses and Surcharges excluding GST Compensation Cess in Gross Central Tax revenues from 2021 till date, year-wise; and
(e) the quantum and share of tax devolution to States against Centre’s gross revenue Tax, Cess, Surcharges and non-tax revenue during the last five years, State-wise, in absolute numbers and percentage?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government’s petroleum procurement diversification policy has helped in ensuring energy security for the country;
(b) if so, the salient features of the said policy;
(c) the number of countries from which petroleum imports are currently being made; and
(d) the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is considering a new high-speed/semi high-speed rail line project in Kerala instead of the Silver Line Project (Semi High-Speed Rail from Thiruvananthapuram to Kasaragod);
(b) whether the Ministry is planning to prepare a new Detailed Project Report (DPR) for such a new high-speed/semi high-speed rail line;
(c) if so, the details and status thereof; and
(d) the details and current status of the Silver Line Project in Kerala?
SR

(a) total States’ share contributed under Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) during the last five years, State-wise and year-wise, details thereof;
(b) total Central share disbursed under MGNREGS during the last five years, State-wise and year-wise, details thereof; and
(c) the amounts anticipated by the Ministry as the States’ and Central share under the new Viksit Bharat-Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission(Gramin) (VB-G RAM G) Act, 2025, for the next financial year, the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) whether Government is empowered under Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act, 2023) and its Rules to collect or access personal data relating to journalists and their sources by requiring disclosure of information from a data fiduciary or intermediary; 
(b) whether digital information pertaining to journalistic privilege and source confidentiality can be compelled to be disclosed by data fiduciary or intermediary; 
(c) whether any exemptions or safeguards exist under DPDP Act or Rules to protect journalistic privilege and source confidentiality; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of sanctioned posts in each of the All India Services, as on date;
(b) the number of officers currently in position in each of these services, service-wise and cadre-wise;
(c) the number and representation of Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribe and Other Backward Classes in these services, service-wise and category-wise, as on date; and
(d) the number of vacancies in these services, service-wise and category-wise, as on date?

(a) the details of post offices closed and proposed to be closed in Kerala during the last 36 months; 
(b) whether application of minimum distance norms of 1.5km radius in urban areas and 3km in rural areas is inappropriate for a densely populated State like Kerala; 
(c) whether any expert study has been conducted before closures, including on disruption of pension payments, Senior Citizen Savings Scheme and other essential services to senior citizens; 
